docs {
  # IepAssistant.Api

  Bruno collection for the IEP Advisor API (`api/IepAssistant.Api`).

  ## Setup

  1. Open this `bruno/` folder as a collection in Bruno.
  2. Select the `local` environment and fill in the `token` secret with a JWT for a parent user
     (log in through the web app or `POST /api/auth/login` and copy the bearer token). Secret values
     are stored encrypted on your machine and never written to git.
  3. The local API listens on `https://localhost:7200` with the ASP.NET dev certificate — if requests
     fail with a certificate error, disable SSL certificate verification in Bruno's preferences or
     trust the dev cert (`dotnet dev-certs https --trust`).
  4. Set `childId` (and the other id variables) to records that belong to the signed-in parent.

  ## Response envelope

  Every JSON endpoint returns `{ "success": bool, "message": string|null, "data": T|null, "errors": string[] }`.
  Failures use `success: false` with `message`; validation errors from model binding use `errors`.

  ## Coverage

  This collection currently covers the Virtual Advocate + Journal feature set only (Journal, Advocate,
  ParentPrepQuestions controllers). Other controllers are not yet reconciled.
}
